---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cite from '../components/Cite.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <h1>About AlligatorPelican</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p>
      AlligatorPelican tracks the public cost of the Alligator Alcatraz detention facility
      in the Florida Everglades. Every number on this site cites a public source. Claims
      without sources are not published. Opinions are clearly labeled and visually separated
      from factual claims.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Origin of the name</h2>
    <p>
      "Alligator Alcatraz" is the nickname coined by Florida Attorney General James Uthmeier
      for the immigration detention facility on the Dade-Collier airstrip in the Everglades.
    </p>
    <p data-claim="alcatraz-etymology">
      "Alcatraz" itself is a Spanish word for <em>pelican</em>, borrowed in turn from
      Arabic. Spanish explorer Juan Manuel de Ayala named San Francisco Bay's island
      <em>Isla de los Alcatraces</em> — Island of the Pelicans — in 1775. The pelican
      meaning is European, not Indigenous; the Ohlone name for that island was
      <em>Metini</em>, "place of the dead."<Cite id="etymonline-alcatraz" />
    </p>
    <p data-claim="domain-name-inspiration">
      The phrase "Alligator Pelican" — and this domain — was inspired by the Netflix-released
      Last Podcast on the Left episode <em>Pain in the Everglades</em>, in which Captain
      Ed Larson takes the hosts on an airboat tour of the Everglades and discusses the
      facility and the pelican etymology.<Cite id="lpotl-pain-in-the-everglades" />
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
    <p>
      Each factual assertion carries at least one citation linking to a non-retracted source.
      Figures are updated within 48 hours of a credible correction. Retracted sources remain
      visible on <a href="/sources">/sources</a> with retraction metadata — transparency over
      deletion.
    </p>
    <p>
      Full editorial checklist and contribution guidelines:
      <a href="/methodology">/methodology</a> and
      <a
        href="https://github.com/AngryMichigander/AlligatorPelican/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank"
      >CONTRIBUTING.md on GitHub ↗</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      To report a factual error or request a correction, email
      <a href="mailto:corrections@alligatorpelican.com">corrections@alligatorpelican.com</a>.
      Factual errors are corrected within 48 hours of a credible complaint; a correction notice
      is posted on <a href="/changelog">/changelog</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
